'''Mob Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] added in [[Version 3.5 Update|Version 3.5]] and was available during the [[Yakuza Apocalypse Collaboration Event]]. During the event, the player must have bought a movie ticket for Yakuza Apocalypse and on the back side would contain its [[Serial Codes|serial code]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 178
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Mob Cat
|name2 = Yakuza Vampire
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Yakuza Vampire''' at level 10

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, it can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of Cats able to perform it, usually with a lower cost. Mob Cat, however, can be used in {{4c}} stages, where there is considerably less competition. Despite that, there are still lower cost alternatives, such as [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]] and [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
There is no reason to use this form. In non-{{4c}} stages, one can just use [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], with the ability to knockback almost all traits as well as access to plus levels, giving you a very strong Cat that you will never get with this one. Even in {{4c}} stages, you can use [[Li'l Titan Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Jamiera Cat]], which gives the same benefits of Jamiera Cat. Overall, the form is outclassed in every situation you might use it in.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield & User Rank Dump|EvolvedClass = Tanker & User Rank Dump|TrueClass=|UltraClass=}}

